  "id": "COMPOUND:18584 - PROTEIN:5790",
  "verbalization": "Zizyberenalic acid appears to interact with HPAC through a series of molecular pathways involving sialyltransferases. The evidence suggests that Zizyberenalic acid targets a specific sialyltransferase enzyme, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is subsequently targeted by other compounds, including (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol and 2-Methylheptyl propanoate. These compounds all ultimately target HPAC, indicating a potential pathway where Zizyberenalic acid may influence HPAC through the activation or inhibition of these sialyltransferase enzymes. The evidence suggests a possible dependency on these enzymes, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear, as the pathways are interconnected and the role of each intermediate is not fully elucidated.",
